===== REFUTE-LENS SUMMARY (PROV-04)  2026-11-08 =====
Objections raised and their outcome (every tool run above: EA_ALLOW_SHORT_DATASET=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2, 10,000 samples, NON-COMPLIANT; the escape only keeps probes tiny):
1. Stale binary / harness artefact: FAILED. cpp/ea_non_iid sha256 1ad1568c... matches the README; run.sh is bash with labelled JSON reads; the REPRODUCE verifier's rule-7 mutation (logs/verify/PROV-04-reproduce.log) shows its gate can fail; my independent script re-measured hAssessed 1.5157083660394497 (declared 8) and 3.2154882678767365 (declared 4) to the digit.
2. Documented / intended behaviour: FAILED. All three lines are upstream-inherited (printf: 64056aa7 Hill 2022; dead-store errorMsg: d464972 McCaffrey 2024; errorLevel!=0 gate: 97dc6ab3 Celi 2020) and verbatim in tag unrepaired-reference-2026-10-15 (utils.h:368-369, 534-535; test_run_base.h:52-54). The fork's documented decision (test_run_base.h:38-43; FINDINGS-TRACKER F02: "the existing stdout warning are unchanged, and no new warning was added") is about #254's proposed inferred-width "not a mapping" warning; it acknowledges this stdout warning exists and was left alone, and decides nothing about its absence from the JSON. The fork's C08 repair (5c3353f8) edited the adjacent errorClass lines and left the dead store. audits/2026-09-30/novel-findings/agent-reports/restart.md:100 had already noted the warning "is likewise lost"; R-3's repair covered only the read-failure errorLevel.
3. Needs < 1e6 samples or the escape: FAILED. The datamask comparison (utils.h:471-483 / 657-669) is length-independent and never consults EA_ALLOW_SHORT_DATASET. Reachable with compliant input.
4. "-q leak" framing: WEAK, as the REPRODUCE verifier also noted. Usage text: "-q: Quiet mode, less output to screen"; implemented as verbose=0 (non_iid_main.cpp:249-252); the escape banner also prints under -q by design. Accurate but not a breach of a documented promise. The substantive defect is the dead store plus the gate.
5. Direction "neutral / conservative": REFUTED AS A GENERAL CLAIM (holds on the reproducer's uniform fixture only).
   - rand1_short.bin declared 1 vs 8: identical hAssessed 0.6117162047939451 (two-symbol alphabet takes the binary path, #253); the warning prints at 8; signal-only loss for the 1-bit production profile.
   - rand4_short.bin declared 4/5/6/7/8: 3.2155 / 2.4365 / 0.9191 / 1.7528 / 1.5157 -- conservative at every wider width, and non-monotonic in width.
   - skew4.bin (sha256 090dce54..., 10,000 x 4 i.i.d. bits P(1)=0.9, true H_min/symbol 0.608): declared 4 -> 0.3222664364784145 (Compression binds, 4 x 0.0806); declared 8 -> 0.5316591386519378 (= H_original; 8 x 0.0804 = 0.643 no longer binds). The mis-declared wider width RAISES the figure by 65%. Nine of ten bitstring estimators rose after width scaling; H_original is identical at both widths, so H_original is the ceiling. Still below the true 0.608, so not "more than the data has" in this measurement, but the mis-declaration can neutralise the SP 800-90B 3.1.3 n x H_bitstring term ("HI = min (Horiginal, n x Hbitstring, Hsubmitter)", PDF p. 20), and the only signal that the width was mis-declared is the one this defect keeps out of the JSON.
6. ea_iid shares the loss (measured, D1/D2): declared 8 prints the warning on stdout under -q; JSON errorLevel 2 with errorMessage = the IID-failure text, i.e. the warning's errorMsg is OVERWRITTEN there rather than gated. ea_restart not run (needs a 1e6-shaped matrix).
7. Stale-text hazard: the two errorLevel=-1 sites with no errorMsg within 4 lines (utils.h:330, :559) are fopen failures that precede the warning store and set errorMsg after a comment block; no stale path found.
VERDICT: CONFIRMED. Severity by the brief's scale: LOW (reporting). Correction required to the record: Direction is neutral for the defect itself, conservative on the uniform fixture, and RAISES hAssessed (capped at H_original) on a skewed source.
